# Never bake secrets into an image layer. server/.env is gitignored rather than
# committed, but a local one still holds live credentials — and because this
# repository historically tracked one, some of its values are already public.
# Copying either kind in would make the image's defaults whatever happened to be
# on the machine that built it, which is the mistake src/config/publicSecrets.js
# refuses to start production over. Supply configuration at run time instead,
# with -e / --env-file.
server/.env
